    "about": "Teach For America Phoenix is the Phoenix regional presence of Teach For America, a national education and leadership-development nonprofit. The Phoenix region works to expand educational opportunity in Arizona by recruiting, developing, and supporting teachers, tutors, alumni, and community leaders who serve students in under-resourced schools and communities.\n\nTeach For America has worked in Phoenix since 1994. The region has brought more than 2,500 teachers to the area over that time and now includes a large local alumni network. In 2025, Teach For America Phoenix reported more than 1,200 alumni living and working in the region, along with more than 240 teachers and tutors serving in nearly 50 local schools.\n\nThe Phoenix work is shaped by Arizona's education challenges, including teacher vacancies, uneven access to strong schools, and persistent gaps in student outcomes. Teach For America Phoenix emphasizes that Arizona needs leaders who are willing to work closely with students, families, schools, and communities to raise educational achievement and expand opportunity.\n\nThe regional program places corps members and tutors in classrooms serving low-income communities. Corps members commit to teaching while developing as leaders, and many alumni continue working in education after their initial commitment as teachers, school administrators, district leaders, policy advocates, nonprofit founders, entrepreneurs, and civic leaders.\n\nTeach For America Phoenix also highlights the importance of Latino educational attainment in Arizona's future, given the state's demographic change and the disproportionate educational barriers faced by Latino students. Its local network aims to strengthen school and community partnerships, support educators, and build long-term leadership for educational equity across Phoenix and Arizona.",
